  21: ## Observations grounding this plan (2026-10-06, corrected after review r1)
  22: 
  23: - Local Supabase answers at `127.0.0.1:54321` (HTTP 200). Messaging DB suite `__tests__/messaging-db/*` 
(`vitest.messaging-db.config.mts`) and local E2E (`playwright.messaging-local.config.ts`) exist from Phase 4.
  24: - Create route (`src/app/api/messages/create/route.ts`): `clientMessageId` optional; repository 
`createWithClientKey` dedupes on unique index `(sender_id, conversation_id, client_message_id)` (migration 
`20261005000414`); the attachment path creates through a separate transactional RPC (route.ts:310). The Phase 4 
composer sends a key for text, attachment, and voice creates (`message-composer.tsx:223`, `useMessages.ts:284`). No 
attempt generation, fence/lookup route, or expected-sender field. Early validation (route.ts:231) runs before any 
budget is charged.
  25: - Rate limiting: `enforceRateLimit` (`src/lib/auth/rate-limit.ts`) fails open on RPC error (line 48); 
`check_rate_limit` (`20260612190000`) increments a fixed-window counter on every call, including denied ones — an 
attempt counter, not a winning-insert quota.
  26: - `Message` type and feed/Realtime mappings expose no `clientMessageId`; optimistic matching is content/time 
based. Mentions do not exist.
  27: - `mark_conversation_read(uuid, uuid)` is SECURITY DEFINER, executable only by `service_role` since 
`20261004170724`, with no internal membership check; `get_unread_counts` still has default `anon` EXECUTE.
  28: - Typing (`src/hooks/useConversationPresence.ts`): public channel `conversation:{id}`; sends true once and false 
after 2 s idle, remote TTL 4 s; payload carries the auth uid and display name; on channel failure it only clears its 
subscribed flag (line 150).
  29: - Realtime: `useMessageSubscription` exposes `connectionStatus` and backoff for the messages channel; 
`useConversationRealtime` exports `connectionStatus` and does catch-up on confirmed streams, but has no application 
backoff and its health is not consumed. `conversation_members` and `message_read_receipts` are already in the Realtime 
publication. No polling. No IndexedDB/BroadcastChannel; Web Locks only in `src/lib/messaging/desktop-notifications.ts`.
  30: - Membership roster: `conversations.participants` is not updated when a `conversation_members` row is removed; 
browser SELECT on `conversation_members` is own-row only; `POST /api/conversations/join` returns 200 from the stale 
`participants` array without restoring membership (join/route.ts:39).
  31: - Drawer (`MessagingContext.tsx`): active conversation ID persisted in global `localStorage` (not per user); 
open flag not persisted.
  32: - Sign-out: the only reachable in-app control is `EnhancedUserMenu` (`enhanced-user-menu.tsx`, rendered by 
`dashboard-header.tsx:81`); the header's own `signOut` handler is unused.
  33: - Test harness: `playwright.config.ts` project `messaging-drawer` uses a filename allowlist of Phase 4 specs and 
`Desktop Chrome` (bundled Chromium, no `chrome`/`msedge` channel); `messaging-desktop-notifications.spec.ts:27` forces 
`channel: 'chromium'`; the E2E fixture signs in two users plus an optional never-signed-in third; the outage helper 
(`drawer-helpers.ts:465`) closes every Realtime socket; the local server's stdout is not captured for tests. Chrome 
and Edge executables are installed.
  34: - None of these contradicts the SPEC.
