  90: ## T27 — Unknown-outcome recovery through the fence
  91: Reasoning: Review r1 #3, #14: fenced recovery is a separate failure surface from durable enqueue, and AC-040 
needs it.
  92: Task: An attempt that ends without a usable response (network error after dispatch, timeout, 5xx after reaching 
the server, tab closed mid-request) leaves the item unknown; before any cancel, expiry, or redispatch the app fences 
it under a new generation; a stored result resolves as delivered (never cancelled or expired); a not-stored result 
only permits the transition that was requested — cancel and expiry complete without any create, and redispatch happens 
only while the item is still current, eligible, and inside its delivery window; cancel is offered only for items known 
not stored; a fence answered 403 `NOT_PARTICIPANT` (access lost while the item was unknown) makes the item failed per 
BR-005 with its text kept, stops automatic attempts, and is never treated as not stored (no expiry, no cancel) — 
"Tentar de novo" fences under a new generation first, so a stored result resolves as delivered and a not-stored result 
follows the normal rules, and "Apagar" only removes the local item.
  93: Done when: AC-003, AC-038, AC-040, AC-042, and the AC-046 5xx clause hold in the real UI with real routes, an 
unknown item fenced as not stored after its 24 h window expires without any create request, and an unknown item whose 
fence returns 403 is failed (not expired, not delivered, not re-created) for both a committed-but-response-lost 
message and a not-yet-stored one.
  94: Verify by: New E2E specs (network error after dispatch, dropped response after pass-through, gateway 5xx after 
pass-through, held create + tab close + reopen, stored-but-unknown item at cancel and at 24 h, unknown-but-not-stored 
item at 24 h, via test clock; removal from the room before fencing for a committed-response-lost item and a 
not-yet-stored item, then access restored and "Tentar de novo" → delivered once / sent once) pass 3 consecutive runs 
in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
  95: Covers: FR-005, FR-006, FR-009, BR-005, BR-007, AC-003, AC-038, AC-040, AC-042, AC-046
  96: Root: T27
  97: Depends on: T8
