  99: ## T10 — Cross-tab outbox ownership and leases
 100: Reasoning: Multi-tab exactly-once (R1-q16 B) is the riskiest client protocol; proven right after fenced 
recovery, before unrelated features.
 101: Task: All tabs of the same user share the outbox and show each item once; per conversation only the oldest 
unresolved item is eligible and one tab holds an atomic drain claim (lease: request timeout 30 s, lease 45 s) that 
ends on tab close/crash or expiry, after which another tab fences and resumes; when connectivity returns, an attempt 
started before or during the outage is superseded immediately under a new generation without waiting for the timeout 
or lease; no two create requests of one conversation overlap across tabs; cancel is atomic against claims and 
propagates to every tab.
 102: Done when: AC-005, AC-006, AC-041, and the AC-045 E2E cases hold with two real tabs, including an attempt 
started during an active outage delivered within 10 s of recovery.
 103: Verify by: New E2E specs (two tabs, held create, tab close, hung lease, attempt dispatched during outage, 
simultaneous online, cancel/claim race, network-log overlap check) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; 
regression suites pass.
 104: Covers: FR-002, FR-004, FR-005, BR-003, BR-007, AC-005, AC-006, AC-041, AC-045
 105: Root: T10
 106: Depends on: T27
