 108: ## T9 — Definitive failures, rate-limit retry, and expiry
 109: Reasoning: The user-visible failure states (BR-005 definitive, 429 transient, BR-006 expiry) are a separate 
outcome from unknown recovery.
 110: Task: Definitive rejections show the item failed with its text and "Tentar de novo"/"Apagar" and block only 
later items of that conversation; "Apagar" removes it and the next item proceeds; 409 retry resends the content under 
a new key once; 429 and 401-with-valid-session stay pending and retry automatically in order; items fenced as not 
stored 24 h after send become "expirada" without auto-send (a fence answered 403 is a definitive failure, never "not 
stored" — T27); manual retry of an expired item keeps the key and the original send time and opens a new 24 h window 
under the normal rules.
