spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/state.md:343:## T28 note (2026-10-07)

 exited 1 in 245ms:
   1: -- Phase 5 T5 / FR-019, BR-009, AC-019, AC-035
   2: -- (spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience): members-only PRIVATE Realtime
   3: -- topic for a conversation's typing signals.
   4: --
   5: -- Topic name contract (src/lib/messaging/typing-topic.ts):
   6: --   conversation:<conversation id, canonical lowercase UUID>:typing
   7: -- joined with `config: { private: true }`. Any other spelling (upper case,
   8: -- braces, suffixes, the legacy public typing name conversation:<id>) is not
   9: -- authorized. A PUBLIC channel with the same name is a different Realtime topic:
  10: -- members on the private topic never receive what is sent there, and it never
  11: -- receives what members send (proved by
  12: -- __tests__/messaging-db/conversation-typing-topic.test.ts).
  13: --
  14: -- Authorization (realtime.messages RLS, evaluated by the Realtime server when a
  15: -- client joins a private channel, on its first broadcast send, and again when
  16: -- the client pushes a refreshed access token):
  17: --   * phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_receive (SELECT = join/receive) and
  18: --     phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_send (INSERT = broadcast send), both
  19: --     TO authenticated only, extension 'broadcast' only, the row's topic equal
  20: --     to realtime.topic(), private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(topic):
  21: --     the topic must have the exact contract form and the caller must be a
  22: --     CURRENT member — private.is_conversation_member(conversation id), i.e.
  23: --     users.supabase_uid = auth.uid()::text -> users.id -> a
  24: --     public.conversation_members row (T28: memberships are created only by
  25: --     authorized server paths; removal deletes the row and records a
  26: --     revocation).
  27: --   * Both policies also require private.is_presence_auth_session_unfenced(),
  28: --     the exact-auth-session fence every existing private topic applies (the
  29: --     Knock and company presence policies): the Presence logout transition
  30: --     records the signed-out session (session_id claim) in
  31: --     public.revoked_presence_auth_sessions, and that session can then no
  32: --     longer join or send on any typing topic, nor keep a join across a token
  33: --     refresh (re-authorization). Only that logout writes the fence, so an
  34: --     active session is never refused by it. A JWT without a session_id claim
  35: --     or without a users row is refused.
  36: --   * No policy grants the 'presence' extension on this topic: presence
  37: --     read/track there is refused for everyone (typing uses broadcast only).
  38: --   * anon has no policy on realtime.messages at all; service_role bypasses RLS
  39: --     (server only).
  40: --   * Existing private topics are untouched: the Phase 4 Knock policy, the
  41: --     Phase 6 company presence policies and the Phase 8 media policies match
  42: --     only 'company:<id>:knock', 'company:<id>:presence' and
  43: --     'company:<id>:space:<id>:media:v2' (checked against the catalog before
  44: --     writing this file); none of their predicates can match a
  45: --     'conversation:...' topic, and the new predicates cannot match theirs, so
  46: --     the OR of permissive policies authorizes no new principal on either side.
  47: --     No existing policy is dropped, altered or reordered.
  48: --
  49: -- Residual risk (SPEC D3, D6; BR-009): Realtime caches a channel's read/write
  50: -- authorization for the life of the join; a member removed while subscribed
  51: -- keeps that join until the server re-authorizes it (refreshed access token
  52: -- pushed by the client) or the token expires. The application leaves the topic
  53: -- on its own removal signal (T15); a tampered client is bounded by the
  54: -- access-token lifetime.
  55: --
  56: -- private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(text) is SECURITY INVOKER (it
  57: -- needs no privilege of its own; the membership read is done by the existing
  58: -- SECURITY DEFINER private.is_conversation_member), search_path '' with
  59: -- qualified names, EXECUTE for authenticated only (Supabase default privileges
  60: -- would otherwise grant it more widely). Policies are evaluated once per join /
  61: -- first send / token refresh, not per delivered message; the membership lookup
  62: -- uses the unique index (conversation_id, user_id).
  63: --
  64: -- Database impact: realtime.messages gains two policies; no table, column,
  65: -- row or grant changes. The CREATE POLICY statements lock realtime.messages
  66: -- briefly; lock_timeout makes the migration fail fast (and be re-run) instead
  67: -- of queueing behind the Realtime server's authorization inserts.
  68: -- Rollout order: this migration first, then any build that joins the private
  69: -- typing topic (T15). Builds before T15 keep using the public
  70: -- 'conversation:<id>' channel, which this migration does not change.
  71: --
  72: -- Rollback (order, SPEC BR-014): FIRST roll the application back to a build
  73: -- that does not join the private typing topic (any build before T15), THEN run
  74: -- this SQL as-is. While no T15+ build is deployed against the target the app
  75: -- step is a no-op. No data is lost (no rows are written by this migration).
  76: --   begin;
  77: --   set local lock_timeout = '5s';
  78: --   drop policy if exists phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_send on realtime.messages;
  79: --   drop policy if exists phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_receive on realtime.messages;
  80: --   drop function if exists private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(text);
  81: --   delete from supabase_migrations.schema_migrations where version = '20261007224737';
  82: --   commit;
  83: 
  84: begin;
  85: 
  86: set local lock_timeout = '5s';
  87: 
  88: create or replace function private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(p_topic text)
  89: returns boolean
  90: language plpgsql
  91: stable
  92: security invoker
  93: set search_path = ''
  94: as $$
  95: declare
  96:   v_parts text[];
  97: begin
  98:   if p_topic is null then
  99:     return false;
 100:   end if;
 101:   -- Exact contract form only: lowercase hex UUID (the canonical uuid::text
 102:   -- spelling), no prefix, no suffix.
 103:   v_parts := pg_catalog.regexp_match(
 104:     p_topic,
 105:     '^conversation:([0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}):typing$'
 106:   );
 107:   if v_parts is null then
 108:     return false;
 109:   end if;
 110:   return coalesce(private.is_conversation_member(v_parts[1]::uuid), false);
 111: end;
 112: $$;
 113: 
 114: comment on function private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(text) is
 115:   'Phase 5 T5: true only for the exact private typing topic conversation:<lowercase uuid>:typing of a 
conversation the caller (auth.uid() -> users.supabase_uid -> users.id) is a current member of.';
 116: 
 117: revoke all on function private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(text) from public, anon, authenticated, 
service_role;
 118: grant execute on function private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(text) to authenticated;
 119: 
 120: drop policy if exists phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_receive on realtime.messages;
 121: create policy phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_receive
 122:   on realtime.messages
 123:   as permissive
 124:   for select
 125:   to authenticated
 126:   using (
 127:     extension = 'broadcast'
 128:     and topic = (select realtime.topic())
 129:     and private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(topic)
 130:     and private.is_presence_auth_session_unfenced()
 131:   );
 132: 
 133: drop policy if exists phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_send on realtime.messages;
 134: create policy phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_send
 135:   on realtime.messages
 136:   as permissive
 137:   for insert
 138:   to authenticated
 139:   with check (
 140:     extension = 'broadcast'
 141:     and topic = (select realtime.topic())
 142:     and private.can_use_conversation_typing_topic(topic)
 143:     and private.is_presence_auth_session_unfenced()
 144:   );
 145: 
 146: -- Readback inside the transaction: exactly the two new policies, broadcast
 147: -- only, authenticated only; the seven pre-existing policies still present.
 148: do $$
 149: declare
 150:   v_new integer;
 151:   v_existing integer;
 152: begin
 153:   select count(*) into v_new
 154:     from pg_catalog.pg_policies
 155:    where schemaname = 'realtime'
 156:      and tablename = 'messages'
 157:      and policyname in ('phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_receive',
 158:                         'phase5_conversation_typing_broadcast_send')
 159:      and roles = '{authenticated}'::name[];
 160:   select count(*) into v_existing
 161:     from pg_catalog.pg_policies
 162:    where schemaname = 'realtime'
 163:      and tablename = 'messages'
 164:      and policyname in ('phase4_knock_broadcast_receive',
 165:                         'phase6_company_presence_channel_broadcast_receive',
 166:                         'phase6_company_presence_receive',
 167:                         'phase6_company_presence_track',
 168:                         'phase8_media_broadcast_receive',
 169:                         'phase8_media_presence_receive',
 170:                         'phase8_media_presence_track');
 171:   if v_new <> 2 or v_existing <> 7 then
 172:     raise exception 'PHASE5_TYPING_POLICY_READBACK_FAILED new=% existing=%', v_new, v_existing;
 173:   end if;
 174: end;
 175: $$;
 176: 
 177: commit;
// Private Realtime topic carrying a conversation's typing signals (Phase 5
// FR-019, BR-009). Join and broadcast send on it are authorized in the
// database only for current members of the conversation (realtime.messages
// policies phase5_conversation_typing_*, migration
// 20261007224737_conversation_typing_private_topic.sql). The database accepts
// only the canonical lowercase UUID form, so the id is normalized here.
// Clients must join it with `config: { private: true }`; the same name on a
// public channel is a different topic that members never hear.
export function conversationTypingTopic(conversationId: string): string {
  return `conversation:${conversationId.toLowerCase()}:typing`;
}
