**Verdict: approve for the T5 database slice. No High or Medium findings.**

Two Low findings remain:

1. **Readback guarantee is overstated** — [migration:160](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20261007224737
_conversation_typing_private_topic.sql:160). The guard counts seven expected policy names; additional policies or 
changed predicates still pass. It therefore cannot establish the claimed exact policy baseline for T23. Smallest fix: 
describe it as a name-presence check and explicitly require complete policy/predicate validation during T23 preflight, 
or strengthen the assertion.

2. **The measured revocation residual is narrower than claimed** — 
[test:462](E:/projects/virtual-office/__tests__/messaging-db/conversation-typing-topic.test.ts:462). The stale socket 
sends before removal and after reauthorization, but never between removal and refresh. JWT expiry is never exercised. 
Smallest fix: narrow the measurement claim to stale receiving and refresh-triggered closure, or add post-removal 
cached-send and expiry coverage.

Local read-only checks confirmed the applied migration, function attributes/grants, correct identity mapping, 
rejection of malformed topic variants, broadcast-only authorization, and no bypass through the seven existing 
policies. An unfenced session without a Presence lease remains allowed. Type-check, touched-file lint, and diff check 
passed.

D3/D6 accept cached receive/send exposure until reauthorization or expiry; this matches [Supabase’s documented 
authorization behavior](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/authorization#updating-rls-policies). **AC-019’s 
five-second app departure remains pending T15**, including closed-drawer coverage. Token refresh and the existing 
conversation-list stream cannot supply that deadline by themselves; T15 needs independent membership reconciliation.

No online database was accessed and no files were edited. Historical suite totals, two rollback rehearsals, and 
before/after MD5 equality remain performer-reported; they were not independently repeated during this read-only review.
